## 1. Core objective and context

Build a systematic corpus of Press Information Bureau (PIB) press releases and
catalogue mentions of **Indian government AI deployments**.

Scope decisions already made by the user:

| Question | Decision |
|---|---|
| What counts as a hit | **Any substantive AI mention** (not deployments only) |
| Date range | **2003 – 2026** (archive runs Dec 2003 to present, rolling) |
| Languages | **English only** |
| Method | Iterative keyword expansion, validated against a full corpus |

**Language exclusion is structural, not a shortcut.** Hindi lives at
`archive2/hindirelease.aspx` in a *separate relid space* (~155k vs English
~292k — the same relid returns different releases in each). There is no working
Hindi advanced search: `AdvancesearchHindi.aspx` 404s in both `archive2/` and
`newsite/`. Hindi records that leak into the English index have titles stored as
literal ASCII `?` (server-side Unicode loss, verified at byte level) and bodies
that 302-redirect to a 404. Urdu and Regional have the same problem.

Coverage may be described as *complete for English releases 2003–present*, not
"all PIB communications."

