### Density finding

A stride-250 HEAD survey of the full relid range found **82.2% live**, projecting
**~240,700 documents**, not the ~284,000 originally estimated. ~38,000 relids sit
in large contiguous dead blocks concentrated in relid 118k–215k. Two blocks
totalling ~9,000 relids sit squarely in **2020** (relid 209251 = 2020-05-29) —
possibly a real archive gap in the Aarogya Setu / COVID period. **Unresolved;
the full crawl will give exact boundaries.**

### Parser (validated, unchanged since the crawl began)

Two bugs found in the dry run and fixed *before* the full crawl, so all stored
records are consistent:

- Single-digit minutes (`19:0 IST`) broke the whole date regex — ~9% of pre-2011
  releases would have had no date at all. Date and time now matched separately.
- Some 2010-era releases ship an empty `<title>`; now recovered from the heading
  or body first line, with the fallback recorded in `parse_warnings`.

**Zero parse failures across 68,960 releases.**

