### Recall measurement — the headline result

A 20-probe battery sharing **no terms** with the accepted list was run against
the 13,065 unmatched 2025 releases. 1,185 were hit by at least one probe. A
random sample of 24 was read individually:

| Verdict | Count |
|---|---|
| Clear AI | 1 (`autonomous underwater vehicles`) |
| Arguable | 6 (traffic-speed radar, counter-drone, drone surveillance, drone land-mapping, cognitive warfare, seed-supply automation) |
| Clear no | 17 |

Dominant false positive: **"autonomous body/institute/organisation"** — a
governance term, 9 of 24.

| Reading | Recall |
|---|---|
| Strict (only clear AI) | **98.0%** |
| Generous (all borderlines count) | **87.3%** |

Strongest evidence: probes returning **zero** hits — `computer vision`,
`natural language`, `generative`, `LLM`, `speech recognition`,
`recommendation engine`. Core AI vocabulary coverage is essentially complete;
what leaks through is *adjacent technology*, not AI proper.

